Lung cancer 5-year survival is 57% when caught at stage I but only 4% at stage IV — the entire difference is the stage at detection, not the treatment quality.
Hypertension affects 1.3 billion people but is preventable with known lifestyle interventions; treating it with medication is effective but costlier and requires lifelong adherence.
Mental health prevention programmes in schools show 17–21% reductions in anxiety and depression incidence — comparable to clinical treatment but delivered to entire populations at low cost.
